-- Trial balance as a derived claim (v0).
--
-- This example does not introduce its own program. It declares one
-- derived claim attached to the Example 4 (double-entry ledger)
-- program, demonstrating Morpholog's read-side primitive.
--
-- A derived claim is a governed view. It is not in the claim set,
-- not persisted, not visible to invariants - it is enumerated on
-- demand from admitted claims, by the same kernel that admits them.
-- The report cannot drift from the source because the report IS the
-- source, projected through a stable rule.
--
-- Domain: every distinct account that appears in any JournalLine.
-- Keys: one row per account.
-- Values: balance = sum of debits posted to the account - sum of
--                   credits posted to the account.


derived TrialBalanceRow(account, balance)
    where balance ==
        sum { d | JournalLine(_, account, d, _) }
      - sum { c | JournalLine(_, account, _, c) }
    over JournalLine(_, account, _, _)
